I've been having trouble sleeping these past few weeks.

184
00:08:46,090 --> 00:08:48,750
I usually lie in bed for hours trying to get to sleep.

185
00:08:49,550 --> 00:08:52,690
I've tried stretching and different breathing techniques before going to bed.

186
00:08:53,470 --> 00:08:55,510
I've tried eating and not eating different foods.

187
00:08:56,610 --> 00:08:57,850
I've even tried counting sheep.

188
00:08:58,590 --> 00:09:02,630
And then when I finally get to sleep, I have these really disturbing nightmares.

189
00:09:03,270 --> 00:09:06,610
So I usually wake up in a panic and more tired than before I went to sleep.

190
00:09:07,070 --> 00:09:07,270
Wow.

191
00:09:08,520 --> 00:09:10,460
Maybe you should get that checked out.

192
00:09:10,460 --> 00:09:10,930
Maybe you're stressed.

193
00:09:12,160 --> 00:09:13,050
Just take some sedatives.

194
00:09:13,640 --> 00:09:13,910
Works for me.

195
00:09:15,140 --> 00:09:18,650
Every so often having some melatonin on hand helps me when I have trouble sleeping.

196
00:09:19,540 --> 00:09:20,970
It works on all kinds of sleeping disorders.

197
00:09:21,680 --> 00:09:24,500
It's the stuff pilots use to regulate their sleeping patterns.

198
00:09:25,140 --> 00:09:25,940
I heard of that.

199
00:09:26,200 --> 00:09:28,280
But does that apply to Alex's situation?

200
00:09:28,980 --> 00:09:29,700
Yeah, sure.

201
00:09:30,280 --> 00:09:31,280
Why not?

202
00:09:31,280 --> 00:09:35,140
Sounds like he only has transient insomnia since it's a recent thing.

203
00:09:35,440 --> 00:09:36,960
So taking melatonin should do the trick.

204
00:09:37,620 --> 00:09:40,400
But shouldn't he be looking into why it's been happening?

205
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:42,420
Well, aren't you the little psychologist?

206
00:09:43,760 --> 00:09:45,000
Our buddy's having trouble sleeping.

207
00:09:45,400 --> 00:09:46,400
It's easy and curable.

208
00:09:46,880 --> 00:09:49,460
It's not something freakish like if he was a sleepwalker.

209
00:09:50,280 --> 00:09:51,670
Well, there's that too.

210
00:09:55,440 --> 00:09:56,140
All right, we're back.

211
00:09:56,400 --> 00:10:00,600
So now we have three main phrases for Fluency Builder.

212
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:01,780
Why don't we start with the first one?

213
00:10:02,160 --> 00:10:02,620
Okay.

214
00:10:02,620 --> 00:10:07,600
So you heard in today's dialogue an interesting phrase.

215
00:10:07,840 --> 00:10:15,620
I don't know if it exists in other languages, but in English we say when you're trying to fall asleep, there's a good technique to help you do so.

216
00:10:15,900 --> 00:10:16,960
You count sheep.

217
00:10:17,540 --> 00:10:19,360
Yeah, I think you see it in cartoons all the time.

218
00:10:19,480 --> 00:10:27,360
A person is sleeping and over that cartoon's head is a little cloud and you see sheep jumping over a fence, right?

219
00:10:27,360 --> 00:10:35,560
So yeah, basically there's a fence and you say one, two, three, and the process of counting helps relax a person.

220
00:10:35,560 --> 00:10:36,010
And you fall asleep.

221
00:10:36,560 --> 00:10:37,560
Right.

222
00:10:37,560 --> 00:10:40,800
So counting sheep, I guess you're not literally out in a field counting sheep.

223
00:10:40,800 --> 00:10:43,930
You're just imagining sheep in your head and you're trying to fall asleep.

224
00:10:44,130 --> 00:10:44,430
That's right.

225
00:10:44,630 --> 00:10:45,150
Counting sheep.

226
00:10:46,320 --> 00:10:47,320
All right.

227
00:10:47,320 --> 00:10:50,930
And well, one of his friends recommended that maybe he should go to a doctor.

228
00:10:51,600 --> 00:10:55,650
And Jill said that by saying, maybe you should get that checked out.

229
00:10:56,070 --> 00:10:56,410
Okay.

230
00:10:56,960 --> 00:11:08,640
So to get something checked out, to get it checked out, this means to have a professional give you a suggestion or to have a professional look at something.

231
00:11:08,640 --> 00:11:08,820
Exactly.

232
00:11:09,640 --> 00:11:11,580
So maybe you should get examined.

233
00:11:12,320 --> 00:11:13,480
Maybe you should go to the doctor.

234
00:11:14,220 --> 00:11:16,440
This isn't just about disorders, right?

235
00:11:16,560 --> 00:11:17,840
I mean, what if I have a sore tooth?

236
00:11:17,840 --> 00:11:18,420
I could say this.

237
00:11:18,840 --> 00:11:19,840
Right.

238
00:11:19,840 --> 00:11:25,340
So if you have a toothache, I would recommend, maybe you should get that checked out by my dentist.

239
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:26,160
Right.

240
00:11:26,440 --> 00:11:29,600
Or maybe if you have a bad rash, you know, your skin is very red.

241
00:11:29,800 --> 00:11:34,120
I say, Marco, I think you should get that checked out by a doctor.

242
00:11:34,120 --> 00:11:35,120
Exactly.

243
00:11:35,120 --> 00:11:40,620
So to get something checked, to get something examined by a doctor or a professional.

244
00:11:41,040 --> 00:11:42,120
All right.

245
00:11:42,120 --> 00:11:44,260
And the last phrase that we have for you.

246
00:11:45,400 --> 00:11:48,710
So last phrase we have today comes from a suggestion at the end.

247
00:11:49,320 --> 00:11:50,930
The friend suggests taking melatonin.

248
00:11:51,840 --> 00:11:55,270
And he says, listen, taking melatonin should do the trick.

249
00:11:55,920 --> 00:11:56,050
Right.

250
00:11:56,920 --> 00:12:00,090
So if you end the phrase by saying, that should do the trick.

251
00:12:01,080 --> 00:12:04,850
Basically you're saying that should solve your problem, that should help you.

252
00:12:05,240 --> 00:12:06,240
Exactly.

253
00:12:06,240 --> 00:12:08,400
So the trick, you don't have to think about what the trick is.

254
00:12:08,400 --> 00:12:11,010
It's just a way of saying it should fix your problem.

255
00:12:11,320 --> 00:12:21,210
So for example, when someone is fixing my car and they have one more thing to do and it's finished, he says, the car mechanic might say, that should do the trick.

256
00:12:21,630 --> 00:12:21,750
Right.

257
00:12:22,600 --> 00:12:23,760
That means problem solved.

258
00:12:23,760 --> 00:12:27,570
Or maybe you're having, you want to hang a picture on your wall.

259
00:12:28,240 --> 00:12:33,270
So somebody puts a nail in the wall and that should do the trick and maybe that'll hold up the painting.

260
00:12:33,990 --> 00:12:34,190
Done.

261
00:12:34,720 --> 00:12:35,720
Done.

262
00:12:35,720 --> 00:12:36,720
Okay.

263
00:12:36,720 --> 00:12:38,920
So that's a way of saying, that should solve the problem.

264
00:12:38,920 --> 00:12:39,790
This should be the solution.

265
00:12:40,460 --> 00:12:41,300
That should be all.

266
00:12:41,680 --> 00:12:42,680
Okay.

267
00:12:42,680 --> 00:12:43,680
Okay.

268
00:12:43,680 --> 00:12:47,920
So why don't we go back and listen to the dialogue one last time.

269
00:12:53,910 --> 00:12:55,830
Alex, what's up with you?

270
00:12:56,620 --> 00:12:57,130
You look dreadful.

271
00:12:57,850 --> 00:12:58,330
Hey Jill.

272
00:12:59,290 --> 00:12:59,790
I don't know.

273
00:13:00,560 --> 00:13:02,800
I've been having trouble sleeping these past few weeks.

274
00:13:03,580 --> 00:13:06,060
I usually lie in bed for hours trying to get to sleep.

275
00:13:06,880 --> 00:13:10,040
I've tried stretching and different breathing techniques before going to bed.

276
00:13:10,840 --> 00:13:12,820
I've tried eating and not eating different foods.

277
00:13:13,920 --> 00:13:15,200
I've even tried counting sheep.

278
00:13:15,890 --> 00:13:19,970
And then when I finally get to sleep, I have these really disturbing nightmares.

279
00:13:20,610 --> 00:13:23,950
So I usually wake up in a panic and more tired than before I went to sleep.

280
00:13:24,410 --> 00:13:24,610
Wow.

281
00:13:25,840 --> 00:13:27,800
I think you should get that checked out.

282
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:28,310
Maybe you're stressed.

283
00:13:29,480 --> 00:13:30,390
Just take some sedatives.

284
00:13:30,920 --> 00:13:31,250
Works for me.

285
00:13:32,440 --> 00:13:36,010
Every so often having some melatonin on hand helps me when I have trouble sleeping.

286
00:13:36,840 --> 00:13:38,280
It works on all kinds of sleeping disorders.

287
00:13:39,340 --> 00:13:41,880
It's the stuff pilots use to regulate their sleeping patterns.

288
00:13:42,580 --> 00:13:43,260
I heard of that.

289
00:13:43,540 --> 00:13:45,600
But does that apply to Alex's situation?

290
00:13:46,300 --> 00:13:47,020
Yeah, sure.

291
00:13:47,600 --> 00:13:48,600
Why not?

292
00:13:48,600 --> 00:13:52,470
Sounds like he only has transient insomnia since it's a recent thing.

293
00:13:52,760 --> 00:13:54,290
So taking melatonin should do the trick.

294
00:13:54,920 --> 00:13:57,750
But shouldn't he be looking into why it's been happening?

295
00:13:58,090 --> 00:13:59,770
Well, aren't you the little psychologist?

296
00:14:01,070 --> 00:14:02,330
Our buddy's having trouble sleeping.

297
00:14:02,750 --> 00:14:03,710
It's easy and curable.

298
00:14:04,270 --> 00:14:06,790
It's not something freakish like if he was a sleepwalker.

299
00:14:07,230 --> 00:14:09,010
Well, there's that too.

300
00:14:11,120 --> 00:14:17,960
Alright, we're back.

301
00:14:17,970 --> 00:14:22,530
So talking about dreaming, nightmares, insomnia, all of this, what do you do if you can't fall asleep?

302
00:14:23,150 --> 00:14:28,010
I don't really have this problem personally because I could fall asleep anywhere, anytime.

303
00:14:28,690 --> 00:14:32,570
I've heard some people take like warm milk before going to sleep.

304
00:14:32,920 --> 00:14:39,080
Some people take milk, although I also heard that dairy products before bedtime can make you have nightmares.

305
00:14:39,080 --> 00:14:40,080
Oh, really?

306
00:14:40,080 --> 00:14:41,640
Like if you eat cheese before bed.

307
00:14:41,660 --> 00:14:42,400
I've heard that as well.

308
00:14:42,480 --> 00:14:46,440
I've heard that if you have seafood before bed, you'll have nightmares as well.

309
00:14:47,920 --> 00:14:53,250
But actually, have you ever had a dream when you are doing something and you wake up in the middle of that?

310
00:14:54,210 --> 00:14:54,600
Yes.

311
00:14:55,030 --> 00:15:05,410
I remember once I was dreaming, I was drinking a soda and all of a sudden I woke up and I had my hand like in the air, like doing the action of me actually drinking the soda.

312
00:15:05,750 --> 00:15:08,210
Actually sometimes this happens to me when I'm falling asleep.

313
00:15:08,710 --> 00:15:15,430
I imagine I'm on a bike or something and I start to feel myself moving my legs and I wake up and I'm like, wait, wait, what am I doing?

314
00:15:16,130 --> 00:15:21,650
So the brain is very strange, I think, especially in those times when you're kind of asleep and you're kind of awake.

315
00:15:21,970 --> 00:15:31,830
Also when you wake up suddenly, I don't know if other people have experienced this, but you feel like you're falling or something, all of a sudden you just wake up with a shake.

316
00:15:32,310 --> 00:15:33,230
Yeah, your body moves.

317
00:15:33,640 --> 00:15:35,520
Yeah, it's really scary.

318
00:15:35,520 --> 00:15:36,520
Your heart starts to beat.

319
00:15:36,520 --> 00:15:37,520
I don't know why that happens.

320
00:15:37,630 --> 00:15:37,910
It's unusual.

321
00:15:38,830 --> 00:15:41,610
Well, we're curious to know what your sleep habits are.

322
00:15:41,830 --> 00:15:44,290
Do you have a hard time sleeping or are you like me?

323
00:15:44,530 --> 00:15:45,690
It's very easy for you to fall asleep.

324
00:15:46,240 --> 00:15:47,640
Let us know at our website, EnglishPod.com.

325
00:15:48,010 --> 00:15:48,640
All right, we'll see you guys there.

326
00:15:48,640 --> 00:15:53,640
Bye.
